questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an e-commerce platform intermittently throws `EntityNotFoundException` during order fulfillment. The following Spring service method was recently deployed:

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired private OrderRepository orderRepository;
    @Autowired private AuditServiceClient auditServiceClient;

    @Transactional
    public Order createOrder(OrderRequest request) {
        Order order = orderRepository.save(new Order(request));
        CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> auditServiceClient.recordAudit(order.getId()));
        return order;
    }
}


The `auditServiceClient.recordAudit(Long orderId)` method performs an HTTP call to an external service, which immediately fetches the order details from the database using a read-committed isolation level.

You are debugging a production issue where a microservice upgraded to Java 21 migrated from a pooled platform thread model to Virtual Threads via `Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()`. Under moderate traffic spikes, the service completely stops handling incoming requests. Thread dumps reveal that all available `ForkJoinWorkerThread` instances are in a `TIMED_WAITING` or `BLOCKED` state, while thousands of Virtual Threads remain queued in `PARKED` state. You locate the following token-fetching cache in the codebase:

java
public class TokenCache {
    private final Map<String, Token> cache = new HashMap<>();

    public synchronized Token getToken(String userId) {
        Token token = cache.get(userId);
        if (token == null || token.isExpired()) {
            token = externalAuthClient.fetchNewTokenOverHttp(userId); // Blocking I/O
            cache.put(userId, token);
        }
        return token;
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an API aggregator service hangs indefinitely under heavy traffic. The endpoint orchestrates multiple sub-queries using a bounded custom `ThreadPoolExecutor` and `CompletableFuture`:

java
public class AggregatorService {
    private final ExecutorService executor = new ThreadPoolExecutor(
        8, 8, 0L, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS, new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(200)
    );

    public CompletableFuture<AggregatedResult> aggregate(String queryId) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            CompletableFuture<DataA> futureA = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
                () -> fetchA(queryId), executor);
            CompletableFuture<DataB> futureB = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
                () -> fetchB(queryId), executor);

            return new AggregatedResult(futureA.join(), futureB.join());
        }, executor);
    }
}
